# Settings names the persona it offers to switch.
#
# The claim under test is not "Settings draws": it is that the page can answer
# "whose practice is this?" — which it could not before, while still offering
# to change it. So the assert is on the persona's name and the seal, not on the
# heading above them.
#
# Drive with testing/woodshed/run-scenario.ps1, under a scratch LOCALAPPDATA:
# `open_store` mints a vault profile when none exists, so a run against the real
# environment would write to Mark's identity store as a side effect.

log persona line: a sealed session names its persona
settle 3

click .pill Settings
settle 2

# General is the default page, so no second click. The persona line is what
# this receipt exists for.
assert text Practising as
assert text Sealed with
capture 01_settings_persona_sealed

# The row that changes it is still there, and still says what switching does.
assert text Switch persona
assert text own Set, history, and settings
capture 02_switch_row_present

log persona line receipt complete
